note for users "Logical account/profile projection of the existing Profile authority, not a new users collection. Physical account records are in elo_profile.accounts; profile_versions, auth_flows, auth_limits, auth_sessions, password_resets, profile_mutations and capability_mutations remain Profile-owned. No collection rename or auth migration."
note for career_goals "One current goal/chat per account; validated saves automatically move the current pointer. Current goals use owner/version CAS edits. Versioned exploration drafts and temporary structured intake records share this collection. Intake promotes the same document into the current goal; no duplicate original-content copy is saved. Draft role/field may be unknown; confirmed role/field are required. Drafts retain adaptive topic context, current focus/question, total_turns and latest 30 turns. Structured progress and bounded evidence only; no raw JD/CV text."

note for interview_prep_suggestions "Private, owner-scoped AI fills for interview questions/preparation the saved research left empty; replaced per goal version and research revision. Labelled as AI-generated; never shared and never stored in interview_research."

note for role_summaries "Private, owner-scoped AI digest of the About the role cards plus AI-made cards for topics no source covered, replaced per goal version and research revision. Digest bullets cite card items; generated cards are labelled AI-made. Never shared and never stored in interview_research."

note for research_briefs "Private, owner-scoped version 2 briefs retained for the existing API; the web app renders interview_research findings directly for both research tabs and never requests these briefs. Replaced per goal version, research revision and format. Never shared and never stored in interview_research."

note for interview_research "Immutable public-context revisions; shared seven-day reuse. Private career_state links constrain user reads. Operational research_contexts holds leases/cache pointers and kind=round_titles one-attempt short-title results; original round names and immutable research remain intact. OpenRouter native web search acquires evidence by default, with Brave LLM Context as fallback. Operational LangGraph checkpoints expire after 24h inactivity; current goals persist. Unavailable acquisition preserves saved goals/research."


