note for cv_upload_capacity "One journaled CAS ledger; account totals derived from at most 20,000 fixed-shape entries. File locks and generation checks fence publication/deletion; no TTL release of uncertain bytes. Development reset releases only the caller's entries after their CV records and files are removed, including stale entries from earlier resets."
note for cv_model_usage "Journaled daily provider-attempt admission across extraction, routing and clarification. Newer days reset counts; backwards clocks do not. Account-specific OS-locked slots enforce per-account concurrency."
users "1" --> "0..*" cv_conversations : owns private retained history
cv_conversations --> cvs : optional source reference
users "1" --> "0..1" career_state : owns current goal metadata
career_state --> career_goals : exact current goal reference
note for cvs "Evidence may be a source-supported summary; semantic approval is transient. Bounded source-linked other_information retains uncategorised content; extraction dates are optional hints. CV-owned structured evidence, overlays, interpretation and history. UUID IDs and private temporary originals; public reads expose no path or owner metadata. The latest extraction/repair graph checkpoint, including parsed source text, persists separately in cv_extraction_states for restart recovery. Saved evidence and history survive expiry cleanup of the original file. Deletion erases checkpoint content and retains a content-free marker to fence later writes. Deleted sources retain content-free receipts, excluded from reads and saved-record quota."
note for cv_conversations "Nullable CV permits manual-only entry. Bounded messages/action receipts have separate transcript revisions; no automatic history expiry."
note for career_state "Automatic goal saving is distinct from explicit CV confirmation. Stamp binds goal ID/version, selection revision and projection hash. Changes invalidate it without another goal record or deleting CV facts."
note for career_goals "Older UUID reviewed-target documents remain retained history, excluded from canonical ObjectId reads. The stored-shape upgrade drops the retired (user_id, create_key) index; historical documents are kept."

